    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "The show method should only require defining a render style per line, not the entire buffer. The current design forces users to manage buffer-wide logic, resulting in unnecessary boilerplate. What's the rationale behind exposing the full buffer instead of just a line-level renderer?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The show method should only require defining a render style per line, not the entire buffer. The current design forces users to manage buffer-wide logic, resulting in unnecessary boilerplate. What's the rationale behind exposing the full buffer instead of just a line-level renderer?</p>",
    "bodyText": "The show method should only require defining a render style per line, not the entire buffer. The current design forces users to manage buffer-wide logic, resulting in unnecessary boilerplate. What's the rationale behind exposing the full buffer instead of just a line-level renderer?",
